  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking:\n- Upgraded to ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore 2.2.0. Consumers must not reference a different ModelContextProtocol.* version (a mismatch causes a MissingMethodException at startup).\n- IMcpHttpInvoker methods now return Task<CallToolResult> instead of Task<string>. Failed (non-2xx) API calls are surfaced as isError:true instead of a soft error payload.\n\nAdded:\n- Tool and parameter descriptions are pulled from XML <summary>/<param> docs (requires GenerateDocumentationFile).\n- Request fields (DTO properties, nested objects, array items) without a [Description] are described from their XML <summary> at runtime, read from the .xml next to each assembly; an assembly without a readable file is reported with one warning at startup and never stops the host. Off via McpScopeOptions.ArePropertyDescriptionsFromXmlDocs.\n- [McpExpose(Scope = ...)] overrides the scope derived from the HTTP method, on an action or on a whole controller; combined flags require all of them.\n- Route and query values are sent culture-invariantly (ISO 8601 dates) and [FromQuery] objects are expanded into their properties, nested collections included; a type the binder reads from one value (a type converter or TryParse, such as a strongly-typed id) is sent whole, and a [FromQuery(Name = ...)] on a parameter or a property is sent under that name.\n- The package ships the XML docs of its public API for IntelliSense.\n- Action routes starting with \"/\" or \"~/\" are absolute, as in ASP.NET Core routing, and [controller]/[action] tokens are replaced in every route.\n- The request CancellationToken is propagated through generated tools to the API call.\n- Method-level [Route] attributes are supported.\n- URL-segment API versioning: the version from [ApiVersion] is baked into the generated route.\n\nChanged:\n- AddMcpTools registers the tools itself (same discovery as WithToolsFromAssembly, hand-written [McpServerToolType] classes included) and builds them when the host starts, so a tool that cannot be created fails at startup instead of at the first request.\n\nFixed:\n- generator.json is no longer created in transitive consumers (e.g. test projects).",
